      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If you've gotten drain cleaner in your eye, it's essential to flush it right away. Rubbing the eye with a cloth may spread the chemicals and make the situation worse. Instead, immediately flush your eye with plenty of water for at least 15-20 minutes to try and dilute the chemicals. If the burning persists, use the homeopathic eye drops you have, but if the pain is severe, seek medical attention as soon as possible.",
